========================================================================
  PART 7: N(n,0) — HERTZSPRUNG NUMBERS
========================================================================

  N(n,0) = #{NUD perms with NO unit ascents AND no unit descents}
  = #{perms with no succession of either type}
  = Hertzsprung numbers (OEIS A000179)

  Hertzsprung sequence: [1, 0, 0, 2, 14, 90, 646, 5242]

  A000179: 1, 0, 0, 2, 14, 90, 646, 5242, 47622, ...
  Our N(n,0): [1, 0, 0, 2, 14, 90, 646, 5242]
  Match with A000179: True

========================================================================
  PART 8: GENERATING FUNCTION STRUCTURE
========================================================================


  From hook-C: the bivariate GF of the x-tribonacci is:
    Σ F(N,x) y^N = (1 + 2xy + xy²) / (1 - y - xy² - xy³)

  At x=1: denominator 1 - y - y² - y³ has tribonacci root τ ≈ 1.8393.
  At x=2: denominator 1 - y - 2y² - 2y³.

  The W(n) sequence is related to F(n, 2) via the NUD transfer matrix.

  Let me compute the characteristic polynomial at x=2:
    p(y) = 1 - y - 2y² - 2y³ = 0
    2y³ + 2y² + y - 1 = 0

  Roots of 2y³ + 2y² + y - 1 = 0:
    r1 = -0.7203098503+0.7848051609j
    r2 = -0.7203098503-0.7848051609j
    r3 = 0.4406197005+0.0000000000j

  Dominant root: -0.7203098503+0.7848051609j
  |dominant| = 1.0652536886

  W(n) / (dominant^n × n!):
    n= 3: 1.10301037
    n= 4: 1.03544384
    n= 5: 0.95986600
    n= 6: 0.88205811
    n= 7: 0.80941614
    n= 8: 0.74415884
    n= 9: 0.68594040
    n=10: 0.63384653
    n=11: 0.58697541
    n=12: 0.54455954
    n=13: 0.50597458
    n=14: 0.47071698
    n=15: 0.43837832

========================================================================
  PART 9: W(n) AND E[H²]
========================================================================


  W(n)/n! = 1 + CV²(H) = 1 + Var(H)/E[H]²
  = E[H²]/E[H]²

  So: W(n)/n! = E[H²] / E[H]²
  And: E[H²] = W(n) × E[H]² / n! = W(n) × (n!)² / (4^{n-1} × n!)
             = W(n) × n! / 4^{n-1}

  Wait: E[H] = n!/2^{n-1}, so E[H]² = (n!)² / 4^{n-1}.
  W(n)/n! = E[H²]/E[H]², so E[H²] = W(n) × E[H]² / n!
  = W(n) × (n!)² / (4^{n-1} × n!) = W(n) × n! / 4^{n-1}.

  Let me verify:

  n=3: E[H²] from Var+E² = 3 = 3.0000
         E[H²] from W(n)   = 3 = 3.0000
         Match: True

  n=4: E[H²] from Var+E² = 12 = 12.0000
         E[H²] from W(n)   = 12 = 12.0000
         Match: True

  n=5: E[H²] from Var+E² = 1185/16 = 74.0625
         E[H²] from W(n)   = 1185/16 = 74.0625
         Match: True

  n=6: E[H²] from Var+E² = 1305/2 = 652.5000
         E[H²] from W(n)   = 1305/2 = 652.5000
         Match: True

  n=7: E[H²] from Var+E² = 1000125/128 = 7813.4766
         E[H²] from W(n)   = 1000125/128 = 7813.4766
         Match: True

